  "summary": "Preprints treat layer-dependent disorder, Kubo-Bastin disorder averaging and non-constant relaxation times, plus a photonic mobility-edge demonstration.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is moving beyond clean-limit or constant-relaxation-time descriptions of transport in topological and orbital-active systems. In twisted bilayer MoTe2, layer-dependent disorder is reported to shape integer and fractional Chern plateau widths and transitions. In an sp3 centrosymmetric square lattice, Kubo-Bastin Chebyshev calculations examine the robustness and tunability of a quadrupole-origin orbital Hall effect under disorder. For multi-Weyl semimetals, a generalized Boltzmann treatment beyond constant relaxation time incorporates orbital moment and intervalley scattering, parameterized by monopole charge N. Related items cover exact mobility-edge phases in 2D photonic quasicrystals, antihelical photonic edge states, and a predicted 2D ferromagnetic Weyl half-semimetal; these are less directly tied to disorder in transport.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
